# Local env
.env
.env.local

# Capacitor — android/ itself is tracked, it's a hand-editable Gradle project. These five
# paths are a deliberate belt-and-braces restatement at the repo root of what `cap add
# android` already put in the generated android/.gitignore (which git honours as a nested
# ignore file and is the authoritative list for everything else it covers — Cordova plugin
# dirs, capacitor.config.json/plugins.json copies, res/xml/config.xml, *.apk/*.aab — see
# that file, not this comment, for the full picture).
android/app/src/main/assets/public
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/build/
android/build/

# Release signing (MC4). android/.gitignore ships #*.jks / #*.keystore commented out —
# uncommented here because a committed release keystore is unrecoverable: it can't be
# rotated without breaking upgrades for every installed user. keystore.properties holds the
# store/key passwords in plaintext, so it goes with them; android/keystore.properties.example
# is the committed template that documents the shape.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
